"\377\377\377\377\377\377\377\377N\001\000\000\000\000\000\000# Welcome to brine! Run this program wi"
"th `brine run`.\012\012fn greet(name: str) -> str:\012    return f\042Hello, {name}!\042\012\012fn m"
"ain():\012    print(greet(\042brine\042))\012\012    # parallel by default: this runs across all you"
"r cores\012    let squares = par [i * i for i in 0..10]\012    print(squares)\012\012test \042greeti"
"ng\042:\012    assert greet(\042you\042) == \042Hello, you!\042\012\000\000";
static _Alignas(8) uint8_t br_s1e348722fbb4fc0e[2336] =
"\377\377\377\377\377\377\377\377\015\011\000\000\000\000\000\000# AGENTS.md \342\200\224 working on "
"`{name}`\012\012This is a brine project. brine is a compiled,\012verified, natively parallel languag"
"e with Python-like syntax.\012\012## Commands\012- `brine check` \342\200\224 type-check and verify "
"(fast; run after every edit)\012- `brine run` \342\200\224 build and run `src/main.br`\012- `brine t"
"est` \342\200\224 run all `test \042...\042:` blocks\012- `brine fmt` \342\200\224 format all source"
"s (always run before committing)\012- `brine guide` \342\200\224 the full language reference (read i"
"t once)\012- `brine explain <CODE>` \342\200\224 explanation of any error code, e.g. `brine explain "
"E0601`\012\012Add `--json` to any command for machine-readable output (one JSON object per line).\012"
"\012## Rules that commonly trip people up\012- `let` is immutable, `var` is mutable; no shadowing.\012"
"- No implicit numeric conversions: write `float(i)`, `int(x)`.\012- Arguments are passed by value. A"
" function that changes the caller's variable\012  declares `ref x: T` and callers write `f(ref x)`; "
"methods use `ref self`.\012- `requires`/`ensures`/`invariant`/`prove` must be proven at compile time"
".\012  If the prover can't, the error lists the known facts; add an `invariant`,\012  a `requires`, "
"or an `assert` (runtime check that becomes a known fact).\012- Inside `par for i in a..b:` you may o"
"nly write outer arrays at `out[i]` (or\012  `out[k * i + c]` with constants `k >= 1` and `c`), and a"
" `par` body can't\012  write files, run processes or read stdin, even through a function it calls.\012"
"- Maps: `m[k]` panics if `k` is missing; test with `k in m` or use `m.get(k)`.\012- No negative inde"
"xes (`xs[-1]` is an error); write `xs[len(xs) - 1]`.\012- Strings index and slice by bytes; `s[i]` i"
"s a one-character `str`.\012- One expression can't change a variable and also read it, or change it "
"twice\012  (`print(xs.pop(), xs)`, `f(xs.pop(), xs.pop())`); split it into two statements.\012  A ca"
"ll inside another call's arguments runs first, so `xs.push(xs.pop())` is fine.\012  Uses on differen"
"t sides of `and`/`or`/`if-else` are fine.\012- Types are optional (`let x = 5` or `let x: int = 5`);"
" if brine.toml has\012  `typed = true` under `[check]`, every `let`/`var`/`for` variable needs one.\012"
"- `match` must cover every case; read enum variant data with `match`, not `.field`.\012- Expected fa"
"ilures return `Result[T, E]` (`Ok(x)` / `Err(e)`) or `Option[T]`\012  (`Some(x)` / `None`); `panic` "
"is for bugs. `x\077` passes a failure up to the caller.\012\000\000\000";
